@baseUrl = http://localhost:5128
@HostAddress = {{baseUrl}}
@companyAdminEmail = admin@al-salamah.com
@companyAdminPassword = User@123456
@missingJob = 3f9a1c22-7b44-4e18-9d05-6c2e8a5f1b70
@missingPayment = 6b2e8a5f-1b70-4e18-9d05-3f9a1c227b44

### =====================================================================
### 19. CLIENT PAYMENT ON A PROJECT (G-1)
### =====================================================================
### Until this shipped, accepting a quotation moved a job straight into execution with no
### financial trace: no entity, no endpoint, no stage. A company put a crew on site without a
### record of what it had received, and "how much is still owed on this job?" had no answer.
###
### Three routes, the same three a company uses to pay the platform, pointed the other way:
### a card through the gateway, a bank transfer evidenced by an uploaded receipt, and cash
### recorded by staff who are holding it. Only a CONFIRMED payment counts against the balance —
### an uploaded receipt is a claim until somebody at the company has seen the bank.
###
### Confirming enough of it releases the project into execution in the same call. There is no
### separate "start work" button, because that is a button somebody forgets, and the failure is
### silent in the worst direction: a client has paid and their project sits in a queue.
###
### The arithmetic — outstanding, required deposit, overpayment, the halala tolerance — is
### covered by ProjectPaymentTests (xUnit). This suite is a smoke test of the surface with
### explicit assertions. Field casing is camelCase (D-8).

### 19.1 Company Admin login
# @name companyAdminLogin
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "email": "{{companyAdminEmail}}", "password": "{{companyAdminPassword}}" }

?? status == 200

@companyAdminToken = {{companyAdminLogin.data.token}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Authentication
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 19.2 Unauthenticated statement -> 401
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/workflow-instances/{{missingJob}}/payments

?? status == 401

### 19.3 Unauthenticated cash entry -> 401
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/workflow-instances/{{missingJob}}/payments/cash
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 1000 }

?? status == 401

### 19.4 Unauthenticated review -> 401
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/workflow-instances/{{missingJob}}/payments/{{missingPayment}}/review
Content-Type: application/json

{ "confirm": true }

?? status == 401

### 19.5 A client's own statement is unauthenticated too -> 401
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/my-requests/{{missingJob}}/payments

?? status == 401

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Not found — a valid request against a job that is not there
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 19.6 Statement for a job that does not exist -> 404
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/workflow-instances/{{missingJob}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Accept-Language: en

?? status == 404

### 19.7 Cash against a job that does not exist -> 404
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/workflow-instances/{{missingJob}}/payments/cash
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "amount": 1000 }

?? status == 404

### 19.8 Reviewing a payment on a job that does not exist -> 404
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/workflow-instances/{{missingJob}}/payments/{{missingPayment}}/review
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "confirm": true }

?? status == 404

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Validation — what the shape check refuses before any money is looked at
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 19.9 A payment of nothing -> 400
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/workflow-instances/{{missingJob}}/payments/cash
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "amount": 0 }

?? status == 400

### 19.10 A negative payment -> 400
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/workflow-instances/{{missingJob}}/payments/cash
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "amount": -2500 }

?? status == 400

### 19.11 A refusal with no reason -> 400
### The client reads this verbatim; "rejected" on its own is not something anyone can act on.
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/workflow-instances/{{missingJob}}/payments/{{missingPayment}}/review
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "confirm": false }

?? status == 400

### 19.12 A one-word refusal -> 400
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/workflow-instances/{{missingJob}}/payments/{{missingPayment}}/review
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "confirm": false, "note": "no" }

?? status == 400

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Authorization — reading a balance is a wider grant than deciding on it
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 19.13 Register a client of this suite's own
### Deliberately self-contained rather than borrowing suite 10's client: the seeded staff
### accounts other than admin@ and deputy@ get Bogus-generated e-mail addresses, so there is no
### deterministic client to log in as, and depending on another suite having run first is how
### one timeout takes four suites down with it.
# @name registerPaymentsClient
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/auth/register-client
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en
X-Tenant-Domain: al-salamah

{
  "fullName": "Payments Suite Client",
  "email": "payments.suite.client@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "+966501234577",
  "password": "ClientSecure@123"
}

?? status == 200

@paymentsClientId = {{registerPaymentsClient.data.userId}}
@paymentsClientOtp = {{registerPaymentsClient.data.devOnlyOtp}}

### 19.13a Verify the OTP so the account can sign in
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/auth/verify-client-otp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "userId": "{{paymentsClientId}}", "otp": "{{paymentsClientOtp}}" }

?? status == 200

### 19.13b Client signs in
# @name clientLogin
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en
X-Tenant-Domain: al-salamah

{ "email": "payments.suite.client@example.com", "password": "ClientSecure@123" }

?? status == 200

@clientToken = {{clientLogin.data.token}}

### 19.14 Client against the staff panel -> 403
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/workflow-instances/{{missingJob}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{clientToken}}
Accept-Language: en

?? status == 403

### 19.15 Client confirming their own payment -> 403
### The whole point of the pending state: a client cannot declare their own transfer received.
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/workflow-instances/{{missingJob}}/payments/{{missingPayment}}/review
Authorization: Bearer {{clientToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "confirm": true }

?? status == 403

### 19.16 Client recording cash -> 403
### Cash is confirmed as it is written, so recording it is the same authority as confirming it.
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/workflow-instances/{{missingJob}}/payments/cash
Authorization: Bearer {{clientToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "amount": 5000 }

?? status == 403

### 19.17 A client's own statement for a job that is not theirs -> 404
### Not 403: another client's project is indistinguishable from one that does not exist.
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/my-requests/{{missingJob}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{clientToken}}
Accept-Language: en

?? status == 404
